  "pr_title": "fix(word): open documents without bringing Word to the front",
  "pr_description": "## Goal\n\nWord stays in the background when spsync reads or saves a SharePoint document that OneDrive does not sync. Users can continue work in another app while a pull, push, or plugin sync runs.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe Word backend opened documents with `open ms-word:...`. LaunchServices then brought Word to the front. `open_url` now passes `-g`, so the app that is in front stays in front. Pull, push, and plugin-triggered sync all open documents through `open_url`, so this one change covers all three.\n\nA manual check with Word 16.115 on macOS 27.0.1 showed that Word does not bring itself to the front when a document opens. Only the launch command did. With `-g`, the foreground app did not change when Word was closed, in front, or in the background. This was also true for the full push sequence: open for edit, change a paragraph through AppleScript, save a copy, and close. A focus-restore workaround is therefore not necessary. The Automation check in `spsync doctor` keeps its hidden launch.\n\nThe change affects only how Word launches. It does not change docx reading, patching, run formatting, comments, or locked content.\n\n`tests/test_word_focus.py` adds an integration test for each Word state: closed, in front, and in the background. The test samples the front app while it pulls the document, pushes an added paragraph, reads the document again, and pushes the original content back. The test checks that the front app never changes, that the added paragraph reached the document, and that the final content equals the original. The test reads a synthetic SharePoint test document from `SPSYNC_TEST_SHAREPOINT_URL` and skips when that variable is not set. Word reports a local document by its HFS path, and `open_url` matches only cloud documents, so the test cannot use a local file. The closed-Word case quits Word, so it skips when Word has open documents.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `uv run ruff format --check`, `uv run ruff check`, `uv run ty check`, `uv run anti-slop-python src tests`, and `uv run pytest` pass.\n- Manual check in Word for Mac 16.115 with a generated local `.docx`: the front app did not change with Word closed, in front, and in the background. The same check without `-g` brought Word to the front.\n- Manual check still needed: run `SPSYNC_TEST_SHAREPOINT_URL=<test document link> uv run pytest -m integration tests/test_word_focus.py` against an unsynced SharePoint test document. This check verifies the SharePoint save and whether Word comes to the front for sign-in or download windows. It has not run yet, so this PR stays a draft.\n\n## Issue\n\nCloses #36\n"
}